The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (zap_drop_file_uffd_wp(details))
    return;

pte_install_uffd_wp_if_needed(vma, addr, pte, pteval);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the code related to UFFD write protection is executed even when the `PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP` configuration is not enabled. This leads to warnings being triggered since the code paths for handling write protection should not be reachable without the necessary configuration.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
#ifdef CONFIG_PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP
if (zap_drop_file_uffd_wp(details))
    return;

pte_install_uffd_wp_if_needed(vma, addr, pte, pteval);
#endif
```
Reason:
The fix involves wrapping the code related to UFFD write protection with an `#ifdef CONFIG_PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP` preprocessor directive. This ensures that the code will only be compiled and executed if the `PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP` configuration is enabled, preventing the warnings from being triggered when the configuration is not present.

